{
  "id": "remove-linked-list-elements",
  "questionId": "remove-linked-list-elements",
  "slug": "remove-linked-list-elements",
  "title": "Remove Linked List Elements",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Linked list",
  "patterns": [
    "linked list",
    "filtering"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "what happens when the very first node needs to be removed - is that a special case for how you'd normally unlink a node?",
    "a common trick with real linked lists is a dummy head node before the real head, so 'removing the first node' looks the same as removing any other node",
    "for our array representation, you don't need pointer surgery at all - just decide, for each value, whether it belongs in the output",
    "walk nums once and append to the result every value that is not equal to val"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "only removing the first matching node instead of all matching nodes",
    "mishandling removal when the head itself matches val",
    "off-by-one errors when multiple matching nodes are adjacent"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A singly linked list is given to you as an array `nums`, where `nums[i]`\nis the value of the i-th node in order, along with a value `val`.\n\n**Remove every node whose value equals `val`, and return the values of the remaining nodes in their original relative order.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= nums.length <= 10^4",
      "1 <= nums[i], val <= 50"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "an empty list",
      "every node matches val",
      "no node matches val",
      "matching nodes at the very start or very end of the list"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [1, 2, 6, 3, 4, 5, 6], val = 6",
        "output": "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]",
        "expectedOutput": "[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]",
        "explanation": "both nodes with value 6 are removed, the rest keep their order"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [], val = 1",
        "output": "[]",
        "expectedOutput": "[]",
        "explanation": ""
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "nums = [7, 7, 7, 7], val = 7",
        "output": "[]",
        "expectedOutput": "[]",
        "explanation": "every node matches val, so the result is empty"
      }
    ],
